 ## shell.css
 
-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-media-query — the shell's layout step follows the viewport width
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15), overridden by the maintainer.
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses a viewport `@media (min-width: 720px)` query.
+- Reason: maintainer decision, 2026-10-23.
+- Known trade-off: the shell also renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen. A viewport query
+  picks the two-column layout inside a narrow pane and clips the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14), which is why the
+  superseded record chose `@container` queries on `.shell`. Revisit if split panes regress.
+
+### §container-not-viewport — superseded 2026-10-23 by §viewport-media-query
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
